# Visual consistency

Use the frozen style in `channel/config.py` for the selected mode. Do not rewrite it per scene.

WTRT = muted historical stick-figure doodle. Money = high-contrast business stick-figure doodle. Takeover = energetic strategic stick-figure doodle.

Not photoreal, not 3D, not anime. Historical names and company names stay out of image prompts (`channel/prompts.py`).

Never put a company or person name in a still **filename** — the model will paint the word onto the picture. HITL stills use index + timestamp (`000_00-00-04.png`). Drop-folder stills use a bracket clock (`[00-00]_….jpg`). Hashed `generate_filename` tokens stay as aliases.

Named public figures must be a recognizable cartoon of the real person drawn as that stick-figure doodle. Reuse `channel/character_locks.json` and pass the hashed photo plus sheet in `channel/character_sheets/` as Google Flow references.

Every still: one idea, one oversized focal object, named lighting, unique staging (`docs/video-engine/QUALITY_BAR.md` / `channel/quality_bar.py`). No filing-table wallpaper.

Still duration is the filename timestamp interval on drop-folder cuts (`[00-13]_….jpg`), or the pause interval from imported audio on the generate path. Long output 3840×2160. ingest-images and drop ingest Lanczos-upscale stills to that size. Shorts 1080×1920.
